---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About Austin Band | Belvedere Decks, Owner-Operated Maryland Deck Builder"
  description="Belvedere Decks is Austin Band's owner-operated deck company serving Maryland from Montgomery County with transparent pricing, honest inspections, and a 5-year written workmanship warranty."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>A belvedere is a structure built to enjoy a beautiful view.</h1>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">
        That is what a deck is for, and it is the bar every project here has to clear.
        Not just built to code. Built to sit on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- TODO: PHOTO - Austin on a finished deck, phone camera is fine. -->
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">I'm Austin Band, and I grew up here.</h2>
      <p>
        I grew up in Maryland building things with my aunt and working in the yard with
        my mom. I still live here, and most of what I build is close to home. Family
        comes first for me, which is most of why I would rather be a company your
        neighbors vouch for than a company that is simply big.
      </p>

      <h2>The long way into this trade</h2>
      <p>
        Economics at the University of Maryland. Coaching high school baseball. An
        apprenticeship under a private car dealer, managing a physical therapy office
        in Rockville, software sales out of Germany. Then decks.
      </p>
      <p>
        It reads like a wandering resume. It was the same job every time: sit down with
        people who are about to spend money, and be straight with them. The car business
        in particular taught me how an industry earns a bad reputation, and what the few
        exceptions do differently.
      </p>

      <h2>How I run this company</h2>
      <p>
        I learned this trade working for other people, and I saw how homeowners get hurt
        in it: work sold before anyone knows how to build it or what it really costs,
        and the difference quietly handed back to the customer. This company is built to
        make that impossible.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing gets sold here that we do not already know how to build. The price is
        built in front of you at your table, not emailed three days later once somebody
        has worked out what to leave out. Permits and inspections are inside the number.
        And I pay my crew properly, which is not generosity, it is quality control:
        crews that get shorted cut corners and then leave, and you inherit both.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you call, you get me. The same person who measures the deck, prices it in
        front of you, and is on the hook for it in writing for the next five years. I
        will walk your existing deck and tell you what I find, good and bad: which posts
        are solid, whether water has gotten in where the deck meets your house, whether
        your frame can carry new boards. If the honest answer is that you need half the
        project you called about, that is the answer you get.
      </p>

      <h2>What every project includes</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>An exact price presented in person, the same visit</li>
        <li>One clear price for the deck we recommend, a straight answer about why, and the same code-perfect structure no matter which boards you pick</li>
        <li>Premium TimberTech and Trex boards, with a straight answer about which line fits your deck and your budget</li>
        <li>Permits and inspections handled where required</li>
        <li>A 5-year written workmanship warranty, on top of 25 to 50 year manufacturer board warranties</li>
      </ul>
      <figure class="site-figure" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <img src="/images/timbertech/badge-timbertech-pro-member.png"
          alt="TimberTech Pro certified installer badge" loading="lazy" style="max-width: 140px; border: none; box-shadow: none;" />
        <figcaption>Belvedere Decks is a certified TimberTech Pro installer.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Where we work</h2>
      <p>
        We cover Baltimore County, Frederick County, Howard County, and Montgomery County.
        If you're elsewhere in the state, call. If we can get to you, we'll build for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The best day in this business is not the day the contract gets signed. It is the
        last walkthrough, when the tools are gone and the people who have been living
        with a construction project in their backyard are standing on the finished
        deck. That is what I am in this for.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first step costs nothing: an honest look at your deck and an exact price,
        same visit, no obligation.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn primary" href="/estimate">Get a Free Estimate</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
